=== Prompt ===
Who is Gandalf?

=== Response ===
Gandalf is a fictional character in J.R.R. Tolkien's high fantasy novel The Lord of the Rings, as well as in the accompanying novels The Hobbit and The Silmarillion. He is a powerful and wise wizard, often referred to as a Maia, one of the Ainur who chose to enter the physical world of Middle-earth.

Gandalf is a central figure in the story, serving as a mentor, guide, and friend to the main characters, especially Frodo Baggins, Bilbo Baggins, and Aragorn. He plays a crucial role in the events of the story, helping the Fellowship of the Ring to destroy the One Ring, a powerful artifact created by the Dark Lord Sauron.

Gandalf is known for his wisdom, courage, and strong moral character. He is also known for his iconic gray cloak, staff, and pointed hat. Despite his powerful magic, Gandalf is not invincible, and he faces numerous challenges and dangers throughout the story. He is a beloved character in literature and has been portrayed by several actors in various adaptations of Tolkien's works, most notably by Sir Ian McKellen in the film trilogy directed by Peter Jackson.

